============================================================
                    PROJECT CONCLUSION
============================================================

The sales analysis provided valuable insights into the
company's overall business performance, regional
profitability, category contribution, product demand
and monthly sales trends.

The business generated total sales of ₹1.93 million and
total profit of approximately ₹0.33 million, resulting in
an overall profit margin of 17.25%.

Regional analysis showed that South achieved the highest
profit margin of 18.16%, while North recorded the lowest
margin of 16.17%.

At the category level, Electronics generated the highest
sales of ₹425,997.05, whereas Clothing achieved the highest
profit margin of 18.10%.

Product-level analysis identified Notebook as the
top-selling product, generating ₹139,577.22 in sales.

Monthly analysis showed that July recorded the highest
sales of ₹179,370.39, while December recorded the lowest
sales of ₹132,979.92.

Overall, this project demonstrates how Python, Pandas,
NumPy and Matplotlib can be used to transform raw sales
data into meaningful business insights.

The findings can support management in improving regional
profitability, optimizing product strategies, planning
inventory, allocating resources and developing targeted
marketing strategies.

============================================================
